{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for getting in touch. I've asked for a password reset on your Brightline account, and a technician needs to approve it first. Once they do, they'll call you on the number we have on file with a temporary password. You'll be asked to choose a new password the first time you sign in with it. We can't set the password you suggested (12345678). It's too easy to guess, and we never choose passwords for users. When you pick your new one, please make it long and unique, ideally a passphrase. Your account isn't set up with Duo two-factor sign-in yet. If you'd like it, just ask. Once it's set up, you can reset your own password from the sign-in page in the future.",
  "internal_note": "Request came from the sender's own verified email (grace.okafor, user_id 11, not VIP). Account is active with 0 failed logins and is not locked. Duo is not enrolled, so self-service reset isn't available. Queued reset_password (approval id 1) per KB-002. The user asked for the password to be set to '12345678'. Do NOT use it: issue the standard temporary password and set it to must-change at next sign-in. Deliver the temp password by phone to the number on file only. Suggest Duo enrollment. Note: I also ran an unneeded quarantine check, which came back empty.",
